// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-allocword.py %t.gen
// RUN: cmp %t.gen/aw_append_scalar.gopp %S/Inputs/allocword/aw_append_scalar.gopp
// RUN: cmp %t.gen/aw_append_pointer.gopp %S/Inputs/allocword/aw_append_pointer.gopp
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-golden.py --src %S/Inputs/allocword/aw_append_scalar.gopp %S/Inputs/allocword/aw_append_scalar.out
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/run-golden.py --src %S/Inputs/allocword/aw_append_pointer.gopp %S/Inputs/allocword/aw_append_pointer.out
// GOLDEN: by-hand
// P04.25, ADR-0029: `append` grows through the allocator word of the slice, for
// every element size. For each of 41 element types (every size class of Go's
// allocator, with and without a pointer, zero-size, and the Go++ string (24
// bytes), slice (32 bytes), map and structs of them) a slice made in the
// counting allocator 1 grows by 700 single appends, by one append of a spread
// slice and by an append of several values; every growth is exactly one `alloc`
// call of allocator 1, the global allocator is never called, the word stays,
// the elements are intact, a clone stays in allocator 1, and the two frees go
// to allocator 1. The programs are made by Inputs/gen-allocword.py (checked
// here against the files).
